d retry makes the push leg non-blocking | 2026-08-11.md | 2026-08-14 |\n| [[concepts/browser-automation-stack-audit-mac]] | browser-harness skipped (routing collision, v0.1.8/257 issues); Interceptor v4.3.0 and Browser v10.0.0 confirmed dead on Mac; two-lane strategy (claude-in-chrome + playwright-cli); neuter-don't-delete plan | 2026-08-15.md | 2026-08-15 |\n| [[concepts/skill-description-budget-ceiling]] | 36 of 150 skills exceed the 650-char ceiling (71,248 chars total) and are silently dropped from the session listing; SkillSystem.md 650 vs CreateSkill 1024 doc conflict; `## Enforcement` relocation as the trim template | 2026-08-15.md | 2026-08-15 |\n| [[concepts/skills-repo-git-hygiene]] | Worktree-routed edits (background-isolation guard), explicit-path staging then `.gitignore` for `.claude/worktrees/` nested-repo hazard, four commits to a clean main, two self-caught mistakes | 2026-08-15.md | 2026-08-15 |\n| [[concepts/session-context-footprint-audit]] | doctor-plus audit: ~21.5k tokens always loaded vs ~3,000 claimed in CLAUDE.md, measured ~7,640-token floor; self-contained HTML report with three-theme-state CSS pre-flight checks | 2026-08-15.md | 2026-08-15 |\n| [[concepts/playwright-cli-install-mcp-disable]] | Playwright MCP ships as an official plugin so `claude mcp` won't remove it — disable at the plugin layer, verify three ways, restart to unload still-loaded tools | 2026-08-15.md | 2026-08-15 |\n| [[concepts/handoff-document-placement-discipline]] | Handoffs written to `/tmp/` are wiped on reboot and invisible to a home-directory search — write to the project directory; ask for the project name not the path; don't start a long subagent task near a usage limit | 2026-08-15.md | 2026-08-15 |\n| [[connections/mandatory-routing-language-outranks-runtime-capability]] | Routing reads descriptions, never the filesystem — dead skills win on \"MANDATORY\" phrasing while working skills are dropped for length; stderr-swallowing preconditions make the former report success | 2026-08-15.md | 2026-08-15 |\n| [[concepts/skills-repo-worktree-branch-cleanup]] | 8 merged worktrees removed but `dcg` rule `core.git:branch-force-delete` blocks agent branch deletion; Telos `[ -w ]`-vs-`[ -r ]` guard gap, 45 unaudited execution.jsonl writers, 5 missing LIFEOS/TOOLS entries | 2026-08-15.md | 2026-08-15 |\n| [[connections/preconditions-that-check-the-wrong-thing]] | A guard detached from its own result (swallowed stderr) and a guard coupled to the wrong property (`[ -w ]` where `[ -r ]` is needed) both report success and fail elsewhere | 2026-08-15.md | 2026-08-15 |\n| [[connections/ground-truth-checks-must-match-the-lying-layer]] | The \"verify at a lower level\" rule needs a direction: identify the transforming layer first, since Windows CRLF makes the working tree lie *toward* difference and `git hash-object` is the check on the far side. | adjudicated | 2026-08-16 |\n| [[connections/bound-the-baseline-window-or-it-decides-the-verdict]] | ACWR counterfactual contamination and the CMJ two-year baseline are the same error — an unjustified reference window silently setting the clinical verdict — running in opposite temporal directions. | adjudicated | 2026-08-16 |\n| [[connections/the-reference-window-decides-the-verdict]] | Zinnecker's baseline narrowing and Tezino's healthy-window control limits are the same reference-window decision, failing in opposite directions | adjudicated | 2026-08-16 |\n| [[connections/refuse-upstream-or-verify-downstream]] | Plausible-looking output is defended against by precondition refusal when a cheap gate exists and by independent-channel verification when it does not | adjudicated | 2026-08-16 |\n| [[connections/install-time-environment-capture-rots-silently]] | Tier C's SDK version skew and memsearch's dead interpreter path are one failure class — a host fact frozen at install time — diagnosed by reading metadata, not running the artifact, and fixed by rebuilding the capture rather than the environment. | adjudicated | 2026-08-23 |\n| [[connections/keep-it-retrievable-not-resident]] | On-ramp distillation and Tier A index trimming are the same lever applied at different layers: cut standing per-session context, never the retrievable corpus or the permanent output. | adjudicated | 2026-08-30 |\n| [[connections/git-repository-boundaries-should-be-explicit]] | A stray home-directory `.git` and near-committed nested worktrees are the same inferred-boundary failure in opposite directions; both fixes replace inference with an explicit declaration. | adjudicated | 2026-08-30 |\n| [[connections/git-scope-errors-inflate-the-work-estimate]] | Phantom 10k changes and a 235-occurrence rewrite were both accurate counts against the wrong git frame — check repo root and remote authority before acting on any bulk count | adjudicated | 2026-08-30 |\n| [[concepts/backup-manifest-drift-and-launchd-status-lag]] | Backup manifest omission (3 project folders) as a distinct `backup-error` class; `launchctl list` column 2 reports only the last scheduled run, so a stale red exit code self-clears and should be left alone | 2026-08-31.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/stale-error-log-archival-discipline]] | `.errors.log` is an append-only escalation channel, not a state record; entries must be confirmed stale against an independent source, then archived before clearing | 2026-08-31.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[connections/status-field-scope-narrower-than-the-question]] | launchd's scheduled-run-only exit code and self-counting comment bumps both report accurately on a narrower predicate than the operational question; check the field's scope before concluding it lied | 2026-08-31.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/dev-knowledge-graph-refresh-2026]] | Adds the quota-strategy and compiler-backlog cross-links alongside the ARMS gaps and scratch-folder references | 2026-09-01.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/codex-adversarial-verification]] | Adds the preregistration and reviewer-unavailability cross-link